{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqfbmoh6tez","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"Zombie loop pileup root cause: soft nudge always says no active loop","summary":"The non-auto soft-nudge path in lib/ready-flag-cache.js readyInjection() unconditionally emits \"No active loop detected — call loop_control start\" on every classify/heartbeat tick, with no awareness of whether a session loop is already active. So every tick on a non-auto-accept session mints a fresh loop_control loop; 12+ zombie loops were observed accumulating in the registry, all spawning the same ready tasks. AUTO mode (lib/loop-autostart.js maybeAutostartLoop) already guards via hasActiveSessionLoop(loops, sessionId); the soft path lacks the equivalent check. Fix: thread hasActiveLoop into the soft nudge and emit a \"loop already active → ScheduleWakeup watch\" branch when true.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-15T14:41:17.419Z","vec":[-0.08575058728456497,-0.024892281740903854,-0.04917239397764206,-0.010304919444024563,0.05906037241220474,-0.05307834967970848,0.012959746643900871,-0.007754303514957428,-0.019290121272206306,0.031510934233665466,0.00021989952074363828,-0.034231383353471756,-0.05768948420882225,0.04648956283926964,0.01788743957877159,0.062487322837114334,-0.011585785076022148,-0.07376531511545181,0.023381583392620087,0.06413591653108597,-0.03995818272233009,-0.06258369237184525,0.11422251909971237,-0.0007323190220631659,0.009663433767855167,-0.003786872373893857,-0.03596080467104912,-0.0703342854976654,0.04451313242316246,0.010410116985440254,0.044680818915367126,0.005227450747042894,-0.02210395410656929,-0.09574729949235916,0.13419799506664276,0.06261178106069565,-0.01853054203093052,0.017182255163788795,-0.04288562014698982,0.020836617797613144,0.04838047921657562,0.008240454830229282,0.0032437278423458338,-0.056196391582489014,-0.025532327592372894,0.01305154338479042,-0.07320626825094223,-0.02830774523317814,-0.051326684653759,-0.030706822872161865,0.0170265